{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5","id":1461465,"title":"The Future of the True Black Hand in V5","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-25T19:25:36-07:00","id":1461465,"title":"The Future of the True Black Hand in V5","content":"One of my absolute favorite sects: the mysterious collection of varying cults; the Antediluvian worshipers who see themselves the stewards of Kindred and mortal alike; those who seek to usher in Gehenna itself: the Tal'Mahe'Ra.<br /> <br /> This is something I bring up whenever the fancy strikes me in various WoD Discord servers and probably annoy a lot of people about. I'm really hopeful that we will have some remainder of the True Black Hand in the future metaplot of V5 because I believe they still have a deep and extremely important role to play in the future of Kindred.<br /> <br /> One of the striking differences about the True Black Hand is that they worship the Antediluvians and that they would see themselves as stewards of Kindred and man, which I stated before. To this, many people probably aren't that impressed with them, but for me, this means quite a lot. I love the idea of worshiping our clan fathers and serving them in different ways and discovering their mysteries. Along with this line of thought, we could be presented with a different history or mythology of how the third generation of Kindred came to be and how/if they truly rebelled against the second generation and [Caine].<br /> <br /> As we know, the Sabbat stands in opposition to the Antediluvians and the Camarilla (until recently) officially denied their existence. However, with the release of the Camarilla sourcebook, our loving sire, Victoria Ash, actually mentions Antediluvian cults in the section on religion and faith in the Camarilla. Unfortunately, she does not edify us much on the subject, most referring to it as ancestor worship (it, in fact, is) and often connected with Gehenna cults and suggests that after the Week of Nightmares, worshiping our clan fathers may not be the best idea.<br /> <br /> Be that as it may, we certainly don't know the will of most of the Antediluvians (or do we?), and some Kindred may indeed find purpose in praying to their respective clan father and wish to connect with their power and what they exemplify. For example, Arikel is hardly ever spoken of negatively among the Toreador. Many of his or her progeny actually speak very highly of her or him (if they are well versed on Arikelite lore).<br /> <br /> Antediluvian worship is hardly just the only feature the True Black Hand has going for it; they have a whole fortress city in the Shadowlands version of [Enoch] with the slumbering Aralu/Antediluvians in the Tempest.<br /> <br /> Currently in V5, I don't think we have the means to traverse the Umbra and go into various realms just yet, but that's honestly not what I want to with the True Black Hand. What I love about them is the extra layer of conspiracy heavily tied to the mythology of the WoD. I'm still in the midst of reading the V20 and original True Black Hand book, so I'll need some time to fully grasp all the plot hooks available to a &quot;Skinlandds&quot; conspiracy of the True Black Hand.<br /> <br /> For those who are more well read on them, how do you see the True Black Hand presented in V5? Would you retcon anything? How could they fit into the direction V5 is going?<br /> <br /> **As an aside, I am unsure if the [Enoch] nuking situation has happened or not, but I also hope that the True Black Hand &quot;being wrong about everything&quot; is also really bad writing.**<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2204-toreador","name":"Toreador","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2204_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T00:16:09-07:00","id":1461492,"title":"","content":"The nuke on Enoch is canon and referenced more than once because of its consequences. So I'm not sure they're going to change that. Generally speaking I don't think the Tal'Mahe'Ra is likely to make a comeback as they never were all that popular.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T01:21:04-07:00","id":1461503,"title":"","content":"I really like the True Black Hand, both as a weird gonzo element and as a more serious Doomsday Cult.<br /> <br /> I feel that, in its weirdness, Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand had somewhat a strong internal consistency, that was a bit lost in the V20 sourcebook: &quot;Tal'Maeh'Rah&quot; is full of awesome ideas, but they feel quite disconnected from each other.<br /> <br /> Why Antidiluvian worshippers would team up with Lilith cultists, after Antidiluvians destroyed the Garden? Why Baali would sing lullabies of sacrifice to keep chtonic monsters sleeping to prevent the end of the world, and then be part of a Sect that wants to awake chtonic monster to end the world? Why, of all places, Faerie Vampires purged by Lasombra mutants would find haven in a sect that actively discriminates against &quot;unnatural&quot; deviations from the original Clans?<br /> <br /> It's a bit like the V20 team wanted to make an early version of CULT OF THE BLOOD GODS, but was prevented from doing so, and put everything into the True Black Hand :-D<br /> <br /> I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> that the current street level setup of V5 (and evident past disdain for the TBH by Revised writers) will probably prevent the comeback of the Hand, at least as a full fledged actor: we may see some noda and winks here and there.<br /> <br /> Nonetheless, there is material coming from past TBH that is perfect for V5.<br /> <br /> In the context of the Gehenna War, at least parts of the Hand would probably go public: perhaps its front-Cults, like the Servitors of Irad and the Ancient Lawgivers, as well as some Revenant families could march to the Ancients' side, and be their foot soldiers and officers in the war against the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Both Camarilla and Sabbat books mention that the war is not just &quot;Sabbat hordes invading Ashirra domains&quot;, but that there is some actual conflict between Methusela cults and Sabbat forces: actually, the Anarchs in Tangiers are mentioned as having joined the Sabbat after having seen what the Ancients can do.<br /> <br /> The Harbingers of Skulls and their wraithly plot can be imported straightly. You can also make the Hecata a bit more cultish and a little less clanish, by bringing in some death cultists of the Hand as members of the Sect.<br /> <br /> The Ahrimanes-Daughters of Cacophony-Lamiae plot can be easily adapted to the more open and widespread Bahari church of V5.<br /> <br /> Considering their nefarious activity in smuggling children to become Chatterlings, the Rafastio revenant family could easily be among the masterminds of the Circulatory System.<br /> <br /> Molochim Baali and Tzimisce could team up with Sabbat Inquisition and become a group of their own: they're the piece of lore most damaged by v5 mechanical changes, as Vicissitude is now an Amalgam of Protean and Dominate, but you could easily recast them as an anti-Infernanalist faction. When the new &quot;Forbidden Religion&quot; book comes out, we will have some new ideas on where Infernalism stands in V5.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 09-26-2021, 04:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T01:24:42-07:00","id":1461507,"title":"","content":"I don't think they're going to bring them back if they arnt going to let you run the second most populus and popular sect in previous editions then it's unlikely black hand is on the cards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T01:28:57-07:00","id":1461510,"title":"","content":"Now that the Camarilla is okay with blood cults, nothing is really stopping any remaining Tal'Mahe'Ra from just joining the Camarilla. I'd just go with that. Most of them are dead and the survivors are setting up new blood cults among the Camarilla and Anarchs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T01:32:28-07:00","id":1461511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1461510#post1461510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that the Camarilla is okay with blood cults, nothing is really stopping any remaining Tal'Mahe'Ra from just joining the Camarilla. I'd just go with that. Most of them are dead and the survivors are setting up new blood cults among the Camarilla and Anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would say it's probable, in a &quot;continuity scenario&quot; with past lore, that many of these Ancient and Methuselah blood cults are run by TBH people, and finally went public.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T02:30:18-07:00","id":1461527,"title":"","content":"Oh hey, people who actually like products from the Andrew Greenberg era! We are rarer than hens' teeth around here. I've long maintained that the original Sabbat line of books developed by Andrew Greenberg and written by Steven C. Brown -- <i>The Players Guide to the Sabbat,</i> the <i>Storytellers Handbook to the Sabbat,</i> and <i>Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand</i> -- form a coherent whole, and you cannot isolate <i>Dirty Secrets</i> as some kind of a black mark on the franchise. The problem with the aforementioned books is that their trajectory goes in a <i>completely</i> different direction from the core of <i>Vampire: The Masquerade.</i> Even now, 30 years later, the current owners of the IP are still trying to figure out what to do with the Sabbat -- to say nothing of the True Black Hand.<br /> <br /> My issue with people who regularly dunk on the True Black Hand (and, more rarely, on the Sabbat as a player option) is that the concepts introduced by Steven C. Brown are only a problem in Humanity-centric, street-level <i>Vampire</i> games. But in the wider World of Darkness? There's nothing in the original vision of the Sabbat that would be beyond the pale in a <i>Werewolf</i> game, and <i>nothing</i> in <i>Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand</i> that would be outrageous in a <i>Mage</i> game. Inhabiting the echo of the First City on another dimensional plane is positively tame compared to what <i>Mage: The Ascension</i> deals with on a regular basis.<br /> <br /> The question then becomes: Does <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> exist in the World of Darkness or not? Do crossovers genuinely destroy the core themes of the game? Are the other titles in the franchise as fragile as <i>Vampire,</i> or are <i>Werewolf,</i> <i>Mage,</i> and the rest in fact more flexible games when it comes to the types of stories that they allow the GM and players to tell?<br /> <br /> My biases are showing, but I don't mind genuine crossovers on occasion. If (for example) the Garou, fomori, the Technocracy, and Nephandi Labyrinths exist (even if only as possibilities) in a <i>Vampire</i> chronicle, then the Shadowlands Enoch, Souleaters, and the Shadow Crusade destroy nothing about the game that wasn't already destroyed by placing the chronicle in the wider World of Darkness in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T02:37:21-07:00","id":1461529,"title":"","content":"I liked the True Hand concept divorced from the Soul Eaters for much the same reason as the OP.<br /> <br /> However, I think that in my head the Baali joining is pretty much a better way to write the sect off than the nuking of Enoch. There were hints that the Aralu were the Baali founders from the beginning but I think if the Children of Ashur have infiltrated the True Hand that you might as well write it off as doomed to corruption.<br /> <br /> I will say that I liked the BJD ideas that they were experimenting with:<br /> <br /> * The True Hand vs. the False Hand with Jalan Aajav attempting to exterminate the former but possibly having bitten off more than he could chew.<br /> <br /> * The True Hand asserting itself as a public sect around Egypt and Carthage. Effectively creating a rival sect to the Ashirra.<br /> <br /> * Being those guys from THE LAST CRUSADE guarding the various tombs of the ancients just as Gehenna starts.<br /> <br /> * Rebuilding without Enoch with the Harbingers and Nagaraja.<br /> <br /> * The Salubri possibly being shepherded by them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T10:52:09-07:00","id":1461573,"title":"","content":"Actually, I've always felt that the TBH may have had a 'hand' in the Prague incident, allowing former members into the greater whole of the Camarilla. Think about it. The True Hand would have the most to gain from a fractured Cam, especially if that would allow their own members to secretly join in. And a 'well-timed' use of Temporsis (new name/powers pending) could explain the Hardstadt death. I have a sneaking suspicion that the Hellenes are actually led by the True Brujah now, and some of the Bani Haqim who joined are actually True Hand too. The Hand could be hedging their bets with allowing Harbingers and Nagaraja enjoining Hecata, but what better way to bend them to their will. Something similar could be happening on the Anarch side, with a few Hand members sneaking in, promoting unrest while keeping the greater part of the sect unaware. As to the the Shadowlands, all trace of the Otherworlds are so far missing in V5. Even Astral Projection was taken away. I haven't read <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i> yet, so I can't say anything about Oblivion vis-a-vis Umbral travel, but from what I've seen, it doesn't exist at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T11:46:27-07:00","id":1461584,"title":"","content":"Also, Enoch may not have been destroyed, yet. With the 20th Anniversary editions, Wraith only exists if the bomb wasn't dropped, preventing the Sixth Great Maelstrom and the ending of the game line. So, if Wraith is still around at least in a similar form to the previous eras, then everything relating to that point may not have happened in the metaplot. This is a possible reason for there not being a Hunter 20th or Demon 20th as both need the Maelstrom to exist as they once did. Technically, Orpheus too, but there seems to have been a retcon addressing that. If Enoch still 'exists' in the Shadowland, and the 20th guide suggests that that may be true, then the True Hand may still have great influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-26T13:05:48-07:00","id":1461599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Toby Weingarten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1461584#post1461584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Enoch may not have been destroyed, yet. With the 20th Anniversary editions, Wraith only exists if the bomb wasn't dropped, preventing the Sixth Great Maelstrom and the ending of the game line. So, if Wraith is still around at least in a similar form to the previous eras, then everything relating to that point may not have happened in the metaplot. This is a possible reason for there not being a Hunter 20th or Demon 20th as both need the Maelstrom to exist as they once did. Technically, Orpheus too, but there seems to have been a retcon addressing that. If Enoch still 'exists' in the Shadowland, and the 20th guide suggests that that may be true, then the True Hand may still have great influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>The X20 lines aren't direct canon continuation despite having <i>some</i> canon continuity built into them. But it'll hardly be used to hard-retcon previous lore in that way. Its main function is to give players new rules for old games, and the reasons behind each new project are more linked to IP discussions and licensing than anything else, as it is an Onyx Path product, but a Paradox copyright licensed in a case-by-case basis.<br /> <br /> If they want to bring back anything from the Dark Umbra they can simply hit forward: the Maelstrom subsumes after a time and something can be recovered, saved by whatever powers. This is fiction, and while pretending some earlier material never happened is bad for reader engagement, you can create any reason (even good ones) to get whatever result you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T10:49:51-07:00","id":1462292,"title":"","content":"I read the integration of the scattered refugee Nagaraja into the Clan of Death as a definitive answer on the current edition's take on the official fate of the Tal'mahe'ra, but that shouldn't stop Storytellers from making the world their own and ruling that things turned out differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T10:22:32-07:00","id":1462566,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think they are really done with it. They were never huge in numbers, and after their base being obliterated in the world of Obliteration, plus their in-fighting, and all that, and let's not forget that many might've just gave up after seeing Ravana go nuts and don't give two damns about them. So I believe most of them would be sad little people who would disperse into the other sects or let themselves be dragged to the Beckoning Zones. Although Camarilla is more probable (and they are needing every potent and old vampire they can get), I can see they running back to Ur-Shulgi, or even trying to destroy Augustus Giovanni as a desperate measure to quell the anger of Cappadocius (if anything from that 'thing' is even left by this point).<br /> All in all though, I see them getting pretty disappointed and miserable, turning to infernalism or other desperations. So... no more True Black Hand. Maybe the Lost Tribe would be back, the V5 Sabbat is very much a back to bases kind of sect, so I can see the Lost Tribe going back to roots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T12:12:18-07:00","id":1462576,"title":"","content":"There's a variant of the Servitors of Irad in Cults of the Blood Gods. I assume that IS the True Hand.<br /> <br /> Page 122-123","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T12:17:17-07:00","id":1462578,"title":"","content":"Shaking my damn head. Who will protect us from the Souleaters now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-03T13:38:38-07:00","id":1462586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1462576#post1462576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a variant of the Servitors of Irad in Cults of the Blood Gods. I assume that IS the True Hand.<br /> <br /> Page 122-123</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Quite a strong Loresheet, by the way.<br /> True Black Hand cultists fighting for paxis, relics and ancient blood against the Sabbat is the perfect setting for some good, old fashioned, Gonzo Vampire Action &lt;3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 10-03-2021, 04:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-04T17:18:31-07:00","id":1462741,"title":"","content":"A story that turns the gonzo dial down to street level could even see a Prince and an Archbishop from two sister cities as fellow cultists secretly in cahoots, maintaining the illusion of a rivalry to whittle down the number of Kindred in one another's domains while they use their respective influences to search for an artifact or ancient grave buried beneath one of their cities. It doesn't always have to be about fighting space monsters from the Penumbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T04:39:37-07:00","id":1462883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1462576#post1462576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a variant of the Servitors of Irad in Cults of the Blood Gods. I assume that IS the True Hand.<br /> <br /> Page 122-123</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> shame any usability of any of the cults is damaged by the Loresheet system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 10-06-2021, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-07T23:43:16-07:00","id":1463064,"title":"","content":"The True Black Hand is a setting element I like to call \u201chigh level Jyhad.\u201d It was one of those groups of string-pullers, like the various Gehenna cults of the Elysium sourcebook, that most vampires never saw. They were even ignorant they even existed (though many vampires obviously must think there are high level conspiracies among vampires of some kind).<br /> <br /> Because those groups are unknown and invisible they can be very hard to implement in the game successfully. But they're totally valid as a setting element.<br /> <br /> Now I actually didn't like Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand when it first came out. It was advertised (or maybe just assumed by the fans) to be about the actual Black Hand of the Sabbat, and what we got... was something else. And there are many gonzo elements that many people just don't like. I, and everyone I knew, was very turned off by it. It just wasn't what we were expecting.<br /> <br /> However, I've slowly gotten around to liking it. Not so much for the actual elements in the book (many of which I still don't like), but for the idea it represented \u2013 that there was more than just interpersonal rivalry in a domain and sect conflicts to vampire. That there were higher conspiracies going on that could still impact the game. Once I imagined it less as canon, and more as an example of what I could do, I saw it more as a toolkit that would be very useful. And I grew to like its imagination and creativity even if I did not use some of the things in it. Between it and Elysium's Gehenna cults though, there is a lot I do use.<br /> <br /> But I don't see how V5 could do it any justice. It (and the Revised metaplot it uses) just jettisoned too many things that made the True Black Hand work. The V5 setting just doesn't support it. At best they'd turn it into a parody of itself \u2013 another sect to be directly fought in the streets instead of mysterious string pullers to be investigated and thwarted by blocking their pawns.<br /> <br /> The interesting things about the True Black Hand and Elysium's Gehenna cults is that they thwarted the expectations of what should be going on. Since the True Black Hand controlled the False Black Hand, it essentially meant the entire Sabbat was a pawn of the antedeluvians. That Gehenna cults like the various Edenic Groundskeepers existed meant there were Camarilla vampires equally devoted to stopping the antedeluvians as the ignorant Sabbat masses. In other words, what you thought was going on in the surface simply wasn't true. There was always another layer.<br /> <br /> That was a wonderful thing for an ST.<br /> <br /> V5 seems to want to take the mystery out of everything. The False Hand being unwitting pawns of the True Hand is interesting. The two fighting each other in the open is boring because its predictable. Making it a public sect instead of a secret conspiracy reduces its usefulness to the ST. It eliminates the concept of a multi-level Jyhad that creates mystery and just makes it another sect conflict which the game already has plenty of. It takes a complex mystery and turns it into a simple thing that can be smashed by brute force. Boring.<br /> <br /> The Servitors of Irad certainly seek to be minions of the antedeluvians. But if they are out in the open, they're just another sect to fight. Not a mystery to unveil. And while the True Black Hand should be involved in it to some degree, I don't think it makes sense for the Camarilla members of the True Hand to be in it. The Servitors should either be pawns of the Hand or ignorant allies with their own agenda separate from the Hand. Likely the members are both. The real True Hand members of the Camarilla should keep their involvement at a minimum. You can't be the string-pullers if you're doing the actual work itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-09T07:58:32-07:00","id":1463223,"title":"","content":"IMO some remnants of the True Hand survived the destruction of Enoch, but they have not yet reformed into a coherent whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T13:38:18-07:00","id":1465032,"title":"","content":"<i>I agree. Lorewise however i dont see why the true black hand wouldnt be around anymore. Notably they consist not just of vampires, some of which proved to survive the unsurvivable many times (Molochim) but they also have Eutanatoi mages and other creatures amongst their ranks and those are definitely still around</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4364,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","user":"Orkar","date":". 10-23-2021, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T13:43:45-07:00","id":1465035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Orkar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1465032#post1465032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. Lorewise however i dont see why the true black hand wouldnt be around anymore. Notably they consist not just of vampires, some of which proved to survive the unsurvivable many times (Molochim) but they also have Eutanatoi mages and other creatures amongst their ranks and those are definitely still around</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, don't worry. As it seems, if I understood it well, I was wrong and they did make a comeback.<br /> <br /> Although it's only a cult for now that only may be composed of original members. What form it will take in the end is yet to be seen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T14:56:52-07:00","id":1465046,"title":"","content":"We now know the fate of the True Hand as the Orphans of Enoch are the ones rebuilding the organization. Given they're a bunch of Elders recruiting newcomers for Gehenna that claim to have been from Enoch until it was destroyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T00:39:07-07:00","id":1465102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1463223#post1463223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO some remnants of the True Hand survived the destruction of Enoch, but they have not yet reformed into a coherent whole.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In my Milwaukee chronicle, Parovich is a Tal'Mahe'Ra dominion (what makes much more sense than a <b><i>Primogen</i></b> as Sabbat infiltrator, imho) trying to use the city's shaky situation and relative isolation to incrementally turn it into a domain aligned with the cult and a new regional center to rebuild the Gehenna cult from.<br /> <br /> (That said, i have yet to decide what kind of form would the cult have in my game and what is Parovich's particular take of its culture and mythology x just rolling the ball from mixing up his agenda with that of the Sabbat NPCs from CbN and the Succubus Club)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-24-2021, 07:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T04:11:59-07:00","id":1465117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1465102#post1465102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In my Milwaukee chronicle, Parovich is a Tal'Mahe'Ra dominion (what makes much more sense than a <b><i>Primogen</i></b> as Sabbat infiltrator, imho) trying to use the city's shaky situation and relative isolation to incrementally turn it into a domain aligned with the cult and a new regional center to rebuild from.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a great idea!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T05:22:50-07:00","id":1465121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1465117#post1465117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s a great idea!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I do like to get an obscure or outdated character here and there to give something of a new spin, specially by using elements of later canon or metaplot, to catch players old and new by surprise.<br /> <br /> My version of Milwaukee has some interconnection with Gary &amp; Chicago, meaning NPCs from either city (not to mention some one-shot NPCs from Blood Bond, Ashes to ashes or the adventures in Succubus' Club) will make the occasional appearance and bring their own shenanigans to the mix.<br /> <br /> <br /> With the occasional twist - Dmitri, the chess-obsessed methuselah &amp; his minions from <b><i>Player of Pawns</i></b> became an all-Lasombra cell of the Amici Noctis, with ties to both Rigaud &amp; Parovich, for example.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or Nicolai's utterly fake <u><i>Apocrypha of Nod</i></u> from <b><i>Child's Play</i></b> being nearly as dangerous as real noddist texts - beware the fanfiction exercise of a $#itposting Occult 7 elder. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-24-2021, 08:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T14:56:23-07:00","id":1465183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1465102#post1465102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my Milwaukee chronicle, Parovich is a Tal'Mahe'Ra dominion (what makes much more sense than a <b><i>Primogen</i></b> as Sabbat infiltrator, imho) trying to use the city's shaky situation and relative isolation to incrementally turn it into a domain aligned with the cult and a new regional center to rebuild the Gehenna cult from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this too. Milwaukee By Night is such an early product that it gets many things wrong as they would get developed later. Other than &quot;evil boogeyman&quot;, there isn't much to the Sabbat in Milwaukee By Night. There's nothing necessarily wrong about the given character, but it's not a natural match for the Sabbat. Making him a member of the True Hand keeps the mystery and essentials of the character, and doesn't require too many changes in the backstory. As a 500+ year vampire, he does fit the profile of a True Hand member, and his part insane/part obsequious rants seem more appropriate for the antedeluvians than the Sabbat. What might be interesting is that Parovich's neonates didn't understand what he meant when they overheard him talking about &quot;the Black Hand&quot;. They can still think he's Sabbat because they don't know he was talking about something else. So Parovich still needs to kill them, and his childer still need to keep hiding.<br /> <br /> Since the True Hand and the Gehenna cults have members within the Camarilla, I also find it a fun exercise to go through earlier products and figure out who would make a good (secret) member of these groups.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T15:11:05-07:00","id":1465188,"title":"","content":"Sabbat infiltrators reaching Primogen positions doesn't strike me as too weird. After all, the purpose of them is to gain power to destroy the Camarilla from the inside and prepare a city for siege.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T16:28:46-07:00","id":1465204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1465188#post1465188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sabbat infiltrators reaching Primogen positions doesn't strike me as too weird. After all, the purpose of them is to gain power to destroy the Camarilla from the inside and prepare a city for siege.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, i find it a little too much - you are one step away from the throne, <i>if not the power behind it</i>, why would you topple <b><i>oneself</i></b>? That's a little <b>too</b> deep for one not to play double agent and go rogue. And it's far from the only inconsistency when it comes to fitting Parovich with the Sabbat as described from the Player's Guide onwards.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1465183#post1465183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this too. Milwaukee By Night is such an early product that it gets many things wrong as they would get developed later. Other than &quot;evil boogeyman&quot;, there isn't much to the Sabbat in Milwaukee By Night. There's nothing necessarily wrong about the given character, but it's not a natural match for the Sabbat. Making him a member of the True Hand keeps the mystery and essentials of the character, and doesn't require too many changes in the backstory. As a 500+ year vampire, he does fit the profile of a True Hand member, and his part insane/part obsequious rants seem more appropriate for the antedeluvians than the Sabbat. What might be interesting is that Parovich's neonates didn't understand what he meant when they overheard him talking about &quot;the Black Hand&quot;. They can still think he's Sabbat because they don't know he was talking about something else. So Parovich still needs to kill them, and his childer still need to keep hiding.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty much how things roll in it - well, except Parovich's brood along with Milo, a childe of Demitri (Merrik's insane Nosferatu hatchet man) and a pair of Caitiffs formed another gang of their own, the Orlocks, with some not-so-stealthy support from Edward Scott, Jason &amp; Decker. Seeing he could not directly hunt them anymore, Parovich ordered bloodbound Raul into making another gang, to serve as his own cat's paws and deal with the matter in his stead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1465183#post1465183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the True Hand and the Gehenna cults have members within the Camarilla, I also find it a fun exercise to go through earlier products and figure out who would make a good (secret) member of these groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fun exercise indeed. Let me give a partial try.<br /> <br /> - Thaddeus, the Nosferatu elder that manipulated the prince of Denver in hunting Jacob Prestor &amp; his childer on Alien Hunger.<br /> - Horace Turnbull, sir Henry Johnson &amp; Edgar Drummond (if one decides to make him smarter than he looks) or Edward Neally in 1st ed Chicago by Night.<br /> - Bronwyn or Cedrick Calhoun in 2nd ed Chicago by Night.<br /> - Louis Fortier in L.A. by Night.<br /> - Elsa Linden in Dark Colony.<br /> - Yokoshi (the whole &quot; visiting japanese vampire&quot; angle is fake), Derek (his obsession with Lupine-killing a cover), Necross (the whole Great Library is a True Hand cell or cult front), or Lyle (the Ventrue's sleeping master is another Aralu) in Dark Alliance: Vancouver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-22-2022, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T16:30:42-07:00","id":1465206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Honestly, i find it a little too much - you are one step away from the throne, <i>if not the power behind it</i>, why would you topple <b><i>oneself</i></b>? That's a little <b>too</b> deep for one not play double agent and go rogue. And it's far from the only inconsistency when it comes to fitting Parovich with the Sabbat as described from the Player's Guide onwards. </div> </div> </div>Mind you, the Sabbat taking over would make you Archbishop but you raise a good point.<br /> <br /> Maybe that's why they made him a Wight in LTSRR","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T04:38:36-07:00","id":1465260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1465206#post1465206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mind you, the Sabbat taking over would make you Archbishop but you raise a good point.<br /> <br /> Maybe that's why they made him a Wight in LTSRR</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Given how high spies have got in real life, their is a lot to be said for what exactly true believers will do for a cause","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T04:53:39-07:00","id":1465262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1465260#post1465260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Given how high spies have got in real life, their is a lot to be said for what exactly true believers will do for a cause</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, not true believers. Parovich wouldn't be the first infiltrator who got very comfortable in their position.<br /> <br /> I imagine the Sabbat weren't about to waste a War Party and Black Hand resources on Milwaukee when they had Chicago nearby. The fact its a Lupine ridden hellhole of battle-hardened veterans doesn't help either.<br /> <br /> So Parovich was probably sitting there idly waiting to be activated until 1999 when everything went to Hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T05:26:08-07:00","id":1465268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1465262#post1465262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, not true believers. Parovich wouldn't be the first infiltrator who got very comfortable in their position.<br /> <br /> I imagine the Sabbat weren't about to waste a War Party and Black Hand resources on Milwaukee when they had Chicago nearby. The fact its a Lupine ridden hellhole of battle-hardened veterans doesn't help either.<br /> <br /> So Parovich was probably sitting there idly waiting to be activated until 1999 when everything went to Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Probably did sit idle, because the tactics and strategy of the Crusades was...strange to say the least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T16:30:17-07:00","id":1465341,"title":"","content":"Parovich wasn't an infiltrator. He was a traitor. His backstory had him as a close friend of the Prince of New York who was there when the Sabbat killed him, and Parovich was allowed to defect instead of being killed. He was working for them as a double agent, with his loyalty secured through the vinculum (not that this term was ever mentioned). Of course, the Sabbat simply planned on killing Parovich after they took Milwaukee.<br /> <br /> And why wouldn't they? After he served their purpose they would naturally dispose of him. Nobody is going to set up a traitor as one of their leaders. He was never really going to be an archbishop. Parovich was stupid for believing they'd let him live, but the nature of his first person backstory narration definitely made him seem to be somewhat crazy so it's not surprising he never figured it out. His reason for being Sabbat was simply because &quot;they were going to win anyway&quot;. He was likely suffering from severe post-traumatic stress. The Sabbat here is just a big scary boogeyman.<br /> <br /> And Parovich wasn't sitting idle. He was trying to keep Milwaukee in continual political chaos so that the domain would be vulnerable to a Sabbat takeover. That was his mission.<br /> <br /> The problem, as I see it, is that there's enough little chinks in the story to not quite sit right. It's hard to see this crazy Nosferatu being a trusted voice on the council. And if Milwaukee By Night was written after the first Sabbat books, they'd probably present him differently to better reflect the Sabbat as it was developed. (Just like how the Sabbat in Blood Bond doesn't seem like Sabbat either - though we could retroactively make them a Nomad pack of Loyalists). In fact, while there are a lot of cool stuff in MbN, any ST running it after 1994 likely would need to change a lot of things to present it in better compliance with the setting. Not too different, but just enough to remove the inevitable &quot;What?&quot; from the players and improve the setting. That's why I'd be totally down with switching things up in terms of who Parovich is really loyal to. You'd have to make changes anyway since you can't run it out of the box.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T18:14:05-07:00","id":1465347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1465341#post1465341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Parovich wasn't an infiltrator. He was a traitor. His backstory had him as a close friend of the Prince of New York who was there when the Sabbat killed him, and Parovich was allowed to defect instead of being killed. He was working for them as a double agent, with his loyalty secured through the vinculum (not that this term was ever mentioned). Of course, the Sabbat simply planned on killing Parovich after they took Milwaukee.<br /> <br /> And why wouldn't they? After he served their purpose they would naturally dispose of him. Nobody is going to set up a traitor as one of their leaders. He was never really going to be an archbishop. Parovich was stupid for believing they'd let him live, but the nature of his first person backstory narration definitely made him seem to be somewhat crazy so it's not surprising he never figured it out. His reason for being Sabbat was simply because &quot;they were going to win anyway&quot;. He was likely suffering from severe post-traumatic stress. The Sabbat here is just a big scary boogeyman.<br /> <br /> And Parovich wasn't sitting idle. He was trying to keep Milwaukee in continual political chaos so that the domain would be vulnerable to a Sabbat takeover. That was his mission.<br /> <br /> The problem, as I see it, is that there's enough little chinks in the story to not quite sit right. It's hard to see this crazy Nosferatu being a trusted voice on the council. And if Milwaukee By Night was written after the first Sabbat books, they'd probably present him differently to better reflect the Sabbat as it was developed. (Just like how the Sabbat in Blood Bond doesn't seem like Sabbat either - though we could retroactively make them a Nomad pack of Loyalists). In fact, while there are a lot of cool stuff in MbN, any ST running it after 1994 likely would need to change a lot of things to present it in better compliance with the setting. Not too different, but just enough to remove the inevitable &quot;What?&quot; from the players and improve the setting. That's why I'd be totally down with switching things up in terms of who Parovich is really loyal to. You'd have to make changes anyway since you can't run it out of the box.</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> <br /> Though I did have a bit of fun with the otherwise disappointing fact that Parovich is a wight in LTSRR. Assuming Parovich was never able to get on a Path of Enlightenment, why do they let a centuries-old vampire wander around killing humans indiscriminately? After all, this is supposed to be the most secure domain in the Camarilla and the Kine are safer there than they are in the vast majority of domains due to Decker's draconian rules.<br /> <br /> Is it some kind of example based rule? &quot;This is what we're fighting?&quot; Or is it because of Parovich that Decker was able to accumulate so much power.<br /> <br /> Or is it simply almost impossible to kill a wight with Obfuscate 5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T21:11:24-07:00","id":1465351,"title":"","content":"Since I haven't read LTSRR, I have no opinion. Maybe it was a bad book? Now given how crazy Parovich seems in MbN, having him become a wight isn't necessarily a bad idea. One can easily imagine it to be a logical consequence of his mental degeneration. But is that truly the best idea to be done with a 500 year old Nosferatu who was a secret Sabbat member?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T21:24:20-07:00","id":1465352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1465351#post1465351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I haven't read LTSRR, I have no opinion. Maybe it was a bad book? Now given how crazy Parovich seems in MbN, having him become a wight isn't necessarily a bad idea. One can easily imagine it to be a logical consequence of his mental degeneration. But is that truly the best idea to be done with a 500 year old Nosferatu who was a secret Sabbat member?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was a fantastic book but I'm biased. Matthew Dawkins loved Milwaukee and probably would have done a whole book if he could have.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T11:57:17-07:00","id":1465428,"title":"","content":"Doesn't the last book of Cult of the Blood Gods: Forbidden Religions have anything that seems a lot like the Tal'MaheRa? I think it did in a way or another. <br /> I also do like the possibility of conspiracy and secret organizations in Vampire, if it done with care and polish, especially if it in street level like V5 mostly sticks with. When things start getting too Global, like wiping out entire cities, nuking spirit towns, having Purgatory fortresses, training camps with revenants and ghouls.... this just is too much for me; it would work for Lord of the Rings or Underworld. But yeah, the mysterious Inconnu, the eldritch True Black Hand (with its religious differences between the Old Tribe, and the Hand Without Sun), the Gehenna Cults... it is a handful of fun to have as an option to tinker with the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-22T12:08:37-07:00","id":1484716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1465204#post1465204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, i find it a little too much - you are one step away from the throne, <i>if not the power behind it</i>, why would you topple <b><i>oneself</i></b>? That's a little <b>too</b> deep for one not play double agent and go rogue. And it's far from the only inconsistency when it comes to fitting Parovich with the Sabbat as described from the Player's Guide onwards.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Pretty much how things roll in it - well, except Parovich's brood along with Milo, a childe of Demitri (Merrik's insane Nosferatu hatchet man) and a pair of Caitiffs formed another gang of their own, the Orlocks, with some not-so-stealthy support from Edward Scott, Jason &amp; Decker. Seeing he could not directly hunt them anymore, Parovich ordered bloodbound Raul into making another gang, to serve as his own cat's paws and deal with the matter in his stead.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A fun exercise indeed. Let me give a partial try.<br /> <br /> - .</div> </div> </div> </div>Lucian, from 1st edition Gary","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-23T16:18:27-07:00","id":1484816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1461465-the-future-of-the-true-black-hand-in-v5?p=1465428#post1465428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't the last book of Cult of the Blood Gods: Forbidden Religions have anything that seems a lot like the Tal'MaheRa? I think it did in a way or another.<br /> I also do like the possibility of conspiracy and secret organizations in Vampire, if it done with care and polish, especially if it in street level like V5 mostly sticks with. When things start getting too Global, like wiping out entire cities, nuking spirit towns, having Purgatory fortresses, training camps with revenants and ghouls.... this just is too much for me; it would work for Lord of the Rings or Underworld. But yeah, the mysterious Inconnu, the eldritch True Black Hand (with its religious differences between the Old Tribe, and the Hand Without Sun), the Gehenna Cults... it is a handful of fun to have as an option to tinker with the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, OPP has already updated the True Hand.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}